<!--
    arm64e __auth_ptr call binding (`option authptrcall on|off`).

    Issue: on an arm64e iOS system daemon every call through an __auth_got slot was
    named, but the three calls clang routes through __auth_ptr
    (`adrp/ldr x16; blraaz x16`, ___chkstk_darwin) rendered
    `(*dat_1000716c0)(...)`. __auth_ptr is a plain S_REGULAR section with no
    LC_DYSYMTAB indirect-symbol entries, so only its chained bind names the
    import.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `loader/kuna_authptrcall.rs`
    names each addend-free bind slot of __auth_ptr after its import and paints
    it Varnode::externref, the `peimportcall` facts, so ActionDeindirect
    resolves the call.

    P0 assertion: `option authptrcall on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; every pass loads
    the `macho_arm64e_auth` fixture (an arm64e PAC00 image, see the fixtures
    README) through the object bootstrap. `_call_auth_ptr` calls through
    `__auth_ptr[0]`, an authenticated bind of `_ext_func`; `_call_table`
    calls through `__const[0]`, an authenticated rebase to `_helper` that the
    chained-fixup resolver unpacks under `dynrelocs`.

    Pass 1 (`option authptrcall off`) reproduces the BUG: the call reads
    `(*_slot_ext)()`, through the slot's own data symbol.
    Pass 2 (`option authptrcall on`, the shipped default) is the FIX:
    `ext_func()`. `_call_table` calls `_helper` in both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
